From 98a138816684c73dd0bb88f823bd5eadf8811aac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Travis Gilbert <1travisgilbert@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:39:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] fix(fork): build the v0.7.0 rebase against the Theorem
 Zed source

Cargo.lock now resolves the GPUI family from Travis-Gilbert/zed 6d4d9075
instead of gpui-pre 0.3.7.

- inline: combine_highlights returns a Vec in v0.7.0.
- node: Paragraph::render binds span again for the link source offset.
- inspector: the Zed source registers the renderer, not a per-window factory.
- settings: flat and sectioned sidebars hold different item types, so each
  is built whole and the two meet as elements.
- shell: fetch_asset answers with the shared load and whether the call
  started it; only an existing, finished load holds an image to drop.
- story: the Zed derive(Action) expands to gpui:: paths, so the crate
  depends on gpui directly.
- tests: the Zed test window has a fixed 2.0 scale and clears debug bounds on
  a cached replay; the two upstream tests run within those limits.
